Subject: [PATCH 0001] Raise cmake_minimum_required from 3.0 to 3.10

CMake >= 4.0 removed compatibility with cmake_minimum_required(VERSION < 3.5),
so Livox-SDK2 fails to configure at all with current CMake (4.4.2 as tested on
macOS 26.5 / Homebrew). Bumping the floor to 3.10 is sufficient; the SDK relies
on no policy behaviour that changes between 3.0 and 3.10.

Applies to all 11 CMakeLists.txt in the tree.
---
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.0)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
 
 project(livox_sdk2)
 
--- a/samples/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/samples/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.0)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
 
 project(livox_sdk2)
 
--- a/samples/debug_point_cloud/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/samples/debug_point_cloud/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.0)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
 
 set(DEMO_NAME debug_point_cloud)
 add_executable(${DEMO_NAME} main.cpp)
